    "appendedText": "\n\n## Intraop acceptance batch 10 ? 2026-11-13\n\nAccepted 13 PASS nodes in 11 whole cases, with ten live cases and one clinic record review. Three salvage cases require unsupported EUA/endocrine families and remain withheld. The manager-excluded polypectomy salvage keeps its review gate. Every new version stays needs_clinician_review.\n\nDefault counts are 1432 cases, 1640 nodes, 1138 registered meanings and 939 scored meanings. Manifest v19 contains 807 rows with JSON SHA256 cf8b57b5786c64af159dc9701285e6bc5670e9fb3c32ce15421efa89e1bfa709. All eleven testing-choice waits and three child/parent/art contexts are registered. The sigmoid combined summary is synchronized to the exact reviewed node explanations.\n\nValidation finished with native exits. Full player 5543/5543, 456 files. Clinical 3508 passed and 11 known failures, 234 files. Domain 6104 passed, 27 known failures and one skip, 224 files. Every residual failure title matches the batch9 baseline. Seven workspace typechecks pass. Lint tests 33/33, focused clinical 161/161, native admission 15/15, focused player 33/33 and excluded-polypectomy source guard 22/22. Accepted cue lint is zero. Pacing PASS at tick 26377 against reference 26281, with zero walkouts.\n\nThe I11 original schema and founder-route pins now reconcile through exact authorized postimages and immutable prior bytes. Historical exclusions retain their captures and assertions. Procedure admission, pediatric gating, format-3/journal completion and stable FSRS identities have passing witnesses. Concurrent App.cloudBrowserFailures.test.tsx work is preserved separately.\n\nHandoff and exact files, bindings, hashes and failure output are in docs/research/question-intraop-acceptance-batch10-20261113.md and its packet, source-freeze, validation and file receipts. Level5 direct bound inputs changed in clinical-content synthetic-content.ts, index.ts, answer-choice-timing.ts and game-domain test-choice-orders.ts. Manifest/data/view are transitive inputs. The manager owns evidence rebind, named clinical sign-off, release and GitHub backup. Local working-tree checkpoint.\n"
